{
  "name": "Zeliks Engine - Follow-up Nudge",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Follow-up nudge\n\nTwo halves. The webhook half is called by the chat entry workflow when a lead has been captured but the conversation has gone quiet; it schedules exactly one nudge (the partial unique index on followups makes a second scheduling a no-op). The timer half runs every 30 minutes, picks up due nudges, sends them, and marks them sent.\n\nNudge text comes from a fixed template with the business name and the lead's need filled in. No AI writes the nudge. One nudge per quiet spell; if the lead replies, any later quiet spell can schedule a fresh one. If the lead books, the pending nudge is cancelled by the booking workflow's status change plus the status filter in the send query.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "4602d051-fafa-4671-be64-064521404d75",
      "name": "Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -120,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "schedule-followup",
        "responseMode": "lastNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "d98f0a55-ad87-49a0-84a2-980489530113",
      "name": "Schedule Nudge (from Chat Entry)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        560,
        140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "INSERT INTO followups (tenant_id, lead_id, conversation_id, due_at)\nVALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4)\nON CONFLICT (tenant_id, lead_id) WHERE status = 'scheduled' DO NOTHING;\n-- $4 due_at is set by the caller: last customer message + the quiet\n-- window from the pack (default 4 hours).",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "f9de93e7-20fc-4fa4-8765-0dbf545168e3",
      "name": "Insert Follow-up (idempotent)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.5,
      "position": [
        780,
        140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "minutes",
              "minutesInterval": 30
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "8fa91c43-4413-4e61-aaab-02b84a732474",
      "name": "Every 30 Minutes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        560,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "SELECT f.id, f.tenant_id, f.lead_id, l.customer_id, l.name, l.need\nFROM followups f\nJOIN leads l ON l.id = f.lead_id AND l.tenant_id = f.tenant_id\nWHERE f.status = 'scheduled' AND f.due_at <= now()\n  AND l.status IN ('new', 'engaged', 'quiet')\nFOR UPDATE OF f SKIP LOCKED\nLIMIT 50;",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "1bfddd09-a13a-4e73-919f-39a7364b988b",
      "name": "Find Due Follow-ups",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.5,
      "position": [
        780,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "abc55825-8032-4147-a8db-601c8a4874d7",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.id !== undefined }}",
              "rightValue": "true",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals",
                "name": "filter.operator.equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "bcbba502-6bc7-481e-8788-e2c26cf24ff4",
      "name": "Any Due?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1000,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "functionCode": "// Fixed template, filled from the pack and the lead. No AI.\n// 'Hi {first_name}, this is {business_name}. You were asking about\n//  {need}. Would you like me to hold a time for you this week?'\n// Spanish-speaking leads get the pack's Spanish version of the\n// same template, chosen by the language of their last message."
      },
      "id": "021c4417-1582-4369-8779-d7bb24b39969",
      "name": "Fill Nudge Template (deterministic)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.function",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1220,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "functionCode": "// PLACEHOLDER - no credentials in this repo, by design.\n// Runtime phase: replace with the tenant's channel send (Telegram\n// bot for this tenant) to customer_id, then pass the item through."
      },
      "id": "40b0ebc5-9359-42f9-969d-a70690c44e65",
      "name": "CHANNEL SEND - PLACEHOLDER (Telegram)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.function",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1440,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "UPDATE followups SET status = 'sent', sent_at = now(), attempts = attempts + 1\nWHERE id = $1;\nINSERT INTO register_events (tenant_id, event_type, entity_type, summary)\nVALUES ($2, 'followup_sent', 'lead', $3, 'Follow-up nudge sent');",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "6a6b5a25-094a-4419-9cb8-7a9fab9c0ef5",
      "name": "Mark Sent + Register Event",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.5,
      "position": [
        1660,
        420
      ]
    }
  ],
